;; The words of AGENTS.md's profile block (RFC-073 "Where agents read it",
;; byj-71w.3). profile/render puts them together from a project's profile:
;; every agent working here reads this block — byj, Claude Code and Codex —
;; and the simulations measured that agents keep to what AGENTS.md says over
;; what a person says in a session (RFC-040). What each axis covers is
;; presets.edn's :covers. {name} is filled from the profile.
{:title "## This project's profile"

 :source "/init writes this block from `.brainyard/profile.edn`, which the person confirmed. No agent changes either: to change the profile, say what should change, and the person changes it."

 :preset "Preset: {preset}."
 :goal "Goal: {goal}"
 :goal-epic "The work toward it is under the epic {goal-epic}."
 :in "In scope: {items}."
 :out "Out of scope: {items}."
 :done "Done when: {items}."

 :levels {:act "An agent here does these on its own, and says so when it hands off:"
          :ask "It does these only with the person's yes. Where a command does it — a commit, a bead filed or closed, a decision record written, a push — it runs the command, and byj asks the person then and waits for their answer; otherwise it asks in its answer and stops:"
          :never "It never does these:"}

 :stop "It stops and asks the person after {limits}, whichever comes first."
 :stop-limits {:failures "{n} failed attempts in a row"
               :usd "${n} spent"
               :issues-per-run "{n} beads filed in one run"}

 ;; bd's block in AGENTS.md defaults to its Conservative profile; naming a
 ;; profile outside it is what agents keep to (byj-aww)
 :bd {:team-maintainer "bd's Agent Context Profiles: this project opts in to Team-maintainer, as far as the lists above go and no further. {push}"
      :conservative "bd's Agent Context Profiles: this project keeps the Conservative profile — agents commit and close beads only when the person asks."}
 :push {:ask "It never pushes on its own; it asks first."
        :never "It never pushes."}}
